course: dictionary
lesson: 14310
title: Abbreviations and typing mistakes
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some long names are shortened to a few capital letters. This is an abbreviation. «The OAS met in the capital to talk about trade.» OAS is short for the Organization of American States, a group of countries in North, Central and South America that work together. Capital letters are a clue that you may be reading an abbreviation.
explain: Now look at «oas» in small letters, with no full stops. It is not a standard English word. Read the sentence around it. If it talks about countries, a group or a meeting, the writer may mean the OAS and not taken care with the capitals. If the sentence makes no sense, it may be a typing mistake.
explain: Always check the context first. «Sam typed oas by accident, so his message looked wrong.» Here oas is a fragment, a small piece of letters that is not a real word. Ask yourself: does this sentence need the name of a group of countries, or does it need a normal word? Then decide, and check with a dictionary if you are unsure.
fact: An abbreviation is a short form of a longer name or phrase.
fact: «OAS» stands for the Organization of American States, a group of countries in North, Central and South America.
fact: «oas» in small letters is not a standard English word, so it is often a typing fragment or a mistake.
fact: Do not mix up abbreviations: «OAP» is the common short form of old age pensioner, not the OAS.
fact: When you meet a short form of letters, check the sentence and the capital letters before you decide what it means.
exercise: «The OAS met in the capital to discuss trade.» What does OAS stand for? | Official astronomy society | Old age pensioner | Open air sports | *Organization of American States
exercise: Which is the correct abbreviation for the Organization of American States? | *OAS | OAP | oas | OAK
exercise: Sam typed «oas» by mistake in his message. What is oas here? | A famous old castle | *A typing fragment, not a real word | The name of a country | The plural of OAP
test: «The news report said the OAS will hold a meeting next week.» What does OAS mean here? | A small town in the hills | An old age pensioner | A type of boat | *A group of countries in the Americas that work together
test: «Ella typed oas in her homework, but it is not a real word.» What is oas in this sentence? | A famous place in London | The plural of an old pensioner | An abbreviation for a group of countries | *A fragment, a mistake that is not a real word
exam: Lily reads «OAS» in a news story about countries in South America. What does it most likely mean? | A petrol station | A type of cloud | *The Organization of American States | An old age pensioner
